edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ is the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186324049 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08b45aef-de01-54a9-97af-2432a20f12ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324061 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324061 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324061 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a13d335-83ee-5413-a2ce-ac3f0bd9be83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324549 #edb/ref 1080 "images/bb/bb82d2af5bba5f24727e80c1e748c9a830d9ea89dde2f641f7cc3062006d94a0.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324549 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324549 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4752b046-3b7e-5b8b-bc64-961b93ceeafa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324658 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324658 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324658 #e